<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#hasDigitalAnalogous> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#hasDigitalAnalogous> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"hasDigitalAnalogous\" property represents a relationship between an entity and its exact digital reproduction. This property is used to link entities to their precise digital counterparts, which maintain all attributes and characteristics of the original. Examples of such digital analogues include a PDF version of a book, a digital twin of a building or city, or an exact 3D reconstruction of a physical object. The \"hasDigitalAnalogous\" property emphasizes the fidelity and accuracy of the digital reproduction in relation to the original entity, ensuring that the digital version tends to serve as an exact representation."@en .
