<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#apelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"appellation\" data property represents alternative names, titles, or designations assigned to an entity, other than the official name. This property is used to specify commonly recognized names, nicknames, colloquial titles, or other forms of identification that serve to distinguish and identify the entity beyond its official designation. Instances are El Greco, Museo Reina Sofía (being the official name: Museo Nacional Centro de Arte Reina Sofía), Big Apple (New York), El Quijote, etc."@en .
