# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Auction
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Auction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Auction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibitionary_Event> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Auction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Auction\" class represents a type of \"Exhibitionary Event\" where artworks, artifacts, or other items are presented for sale to the highest bidder. Auctions are typically organized by auction houses, galleries, or other entities, and they attract collectors, dealers, and the general public."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Auction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "auction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Auction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "subasta"@es .
# 
