# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collective_Human_Actant
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collective_Human_Actant> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collective_Human_Actant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Human_Actant> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collective_Human_Actant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A group of individuals who act together as a collective entity to influence, participate in, or intervene in specific processes or situations. This collective may be formal, such as institutions or professional associations, or informal, such as social communities or an interest group."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collective_Human_Actant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "actante humano colectivo"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collective_Human_Actant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "collective human actant"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collector
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collector> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collector> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Role> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collector> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "coleccionista"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collector> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "collector"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Comment
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Comment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Comment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Comment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A proposition formulated as a comment: a brief, situated—often reactive—statement expressing an observation, evaluation, interpretation, agreement/disagreement, or qualification regarding an entity or situation in the exhibition ecosystem. It is distinct from any specific materialization or carrier (e.g., post, note, or form entry), which is modeled elsewhere."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Comment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "comentario"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Comment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "comment"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Commissioner
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Commissioner> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Commissioner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Role> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Commissioner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "comitente"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Commissioner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "commissioner"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Activity
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Activity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Planned_Activity> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Communication Activity\" class represents any activity aimed at conveying information, promoting events, engaging with audiences, or facilitating interaction and dialogue. This includes a wide range of activities such as public relations campaigns, social media interactions, press releases, newsletters, and other forms of communication that support the dissemination and reception of information related to art exhibitions and cultural events."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "actividad de comunicación"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "communication activity"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Dispositif
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Dispositif> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Communication Dispositif\" class represents materials and events used to communicate and disseminate information about cultural activities and productions. These dispositifs typically include press releases, brochures, websites, social media posts, newsletters, and other structured systems or media that convey information to the public and stakeholders. Additionally, other objects and materials can also serve this purpose. Therefore, this class links cultural activities and productions with those propositional objects and events that inform about them, regardless of their nature, genre, or typology."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "communication dispositif"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dispositivo de comunicación"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Dispositif> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#modelingNote> "This class is not disjoint with other dispositif types; see Dispositif modeling note."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communities
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communities> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communities> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/E74_Group> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communities> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A group of individuals who interact informally moved by shared interests. In the context of the OntoExhibit ontology, this class specifically refers to communities that interact on social media platforms, such as Twitter, Facebook, Discord, etc. This class would include, for example, instances of DAOs (decentralized autonomous organizations)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communities> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "community"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communities> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "comunidad"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Company
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Company> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Company> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F11_Corporate_Body> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Company> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A legal entity established with the goal of obtaining economic benefits. In the context of the OntoExhibit ontology, this class specifically refers to those entities dedicated to the sale, distribution, or promotion of products and services related to art. This may include commercial galleries, art consultancy firms, art supply companies, among others. It also refers to those entities not directly related to the art field, but that can act as promoters or financiers in certain exhibition projects. This class also includes those entities that play a significant role in the field of art criticism, the production/publication of curatorial texts, and, in general, cultural, intellectual, or artistic productions related to art exhibitions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Company> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "company"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Company> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "compañía empresarial"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Complementary_Topic
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Complementary_Topic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Complementary_Topic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Theme> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Complementary_Topic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "complementary topic"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Complementary_Topic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "tema complementario"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Development
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Development> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Development> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/E65_Creation> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Development> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Computational Development\" class represents the activities and processes involved in creating, designing, and implementing computational systems, software, and algorithms. This includes the development of digital tools, applications, interactive systems, and computational models that support various domains such as art, science, engineering, and education. Computational Development encompasses tasks such as coding, software engineering, system architecture, algorithm design, and testing, aimed at producing functional and innovative technological solutions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Development> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "computational development"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Development> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "desarrollo computacional"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Object
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Object> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid199 .
_:genid199 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Development> .
_:genid199 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#hasProduction> .
_:genid199 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Computational objects are treated as propositional objects because their design, modelling and production embed explicit or implicit propositions (e.g., data models, rules, constraints, affordances, policies, and algorithmic logics). This propositional character holds even when such objects also function under other facets (e.g., place or actant)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Computational Object\" class represents entities created with computational languages, and processed or existing within computational systems. These objects include software, algorithms, simulations, virtual environments, AI systems, and other digital productions. Computational Objects are characterized by their creation, manipulation, and existence within digital or computational frameworks, and they play a crucial role in digital art, generative curation, and digital exhibitions. Nevertheless, this class should not be confused with artworks, cultural objects, or other work manifestations that materialize in digital format."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "computational object"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "objeto computacional"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Concept
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Concept> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Concept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/E28_Conceptual_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Concept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A fundamental unit that represents an abstract idea, entity, or category that encapsulates the essential characteristics and properties of an object, event, or phenomenon."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Concept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "concept"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Concept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "concepto"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Concept> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> "https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F6"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conception
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/E65_Creation> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Conception\" refers to the specific activity involved in the conceptualization of abstract, non-material objects. This class encompasses the intellectual processes and creative thinking required to develop ideas, theories, frameworks, and other intangible constructs. \"Conception\" includes activities such as brainstorming, theorizing, imagining, planning, and designing conceptual entities. It is characterized by the formulation of novel concepts, models, or solutions that exist primarily in the cognitive realm, rather than having a physical form."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "concepción"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "conception"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conceptual_Work
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conceptual_Work> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conceptual_Work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/E28_Conceptual_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conceptual_Work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conceptual_Work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The intellectual and conceptual formulation of a work conceived as a coherent and unitary entity in itself. It is potentially susceptible to being realized in various expressions and/or manifestations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conceptual_Work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "conceptual work"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conceptual_Work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "obra conceptual"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conceptual_Work> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> "https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F1" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conference
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conference> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conference> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Scholarly_Educational_Activity> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conference> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "conference"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conference> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "congreso"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conmemorative_Event
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conmemorative_Event> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conmemorative_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#propositional_activity> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conmemorative_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid200 .
_:genid200 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Time_Range> .
_:genid200 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#hasTimeSpan> .
_:genid200 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conmemorative_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Commemorative Event\" class represents a significant occasion organized to honor, remember, or celebrate an important person, event, or milestone, such as the fiftieth anniversary of Picasso's death. A Commemorative Event can encompass a variety of activities and sub-events, including exhibitions, lectures, performances, and ceremonies."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conmemorative_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "conmemorative event"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conmemorative_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "evento conmemorativo"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Consultant
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Consultant> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Consultant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Role> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Consultant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "consultant"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Consultant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "consultor"@es .
