# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Corporate_Body_Unit
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Corporate_Body_Unit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Corporate_Body_Unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F11_Corporate_Body> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Corporate_Body_Unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A functional unit within a corporate organization that specializes in specific tasks or functions, forming part of the corporation's overall structure. This unit may be a department, a division, or any other segment that has defined roles and responsibilities within the corporation. This class may include instances such as: Departamento de Pintura of the Museo del Prado or Vicerrectorado de Cultural of the Universidad de Málaga."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Corporate_Body_Unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "corporate body unit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Corporate_Body_Unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "unidad de organización corporativa"@es .
