# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Critique
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Critique> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Critique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Critique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In OntoExhibit, the Critique class represents a specific type of proposition that constitutes the core content of an art review or critical work. A critique provides an evaluative or interpretative perspective on artworks and exhibitions, offering insights that reflect the author's  analysis or judgment.  This class serves to distinguish the conceptual content  from its medium or context, enabling the analysis of its role in shaping discourses around art and exhibitions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Critique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "critique"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Critique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "crítica"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Center
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Center> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Center> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Institution> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Center> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "centro cultural"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Center> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "cultural center"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Institution
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Institution> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Institution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Institution> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Institution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This class comprises institutions whose main role is the preservation, research, communication and exhibition of cultural productions, such as museums, art centers, foundations, libraries, and other cultural organizations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Institution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "cultural institution"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Institution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "institución cultural"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Work_Manifestation
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Work_Manifestation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Work_Manifestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Work_Manifestation> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Work_Manifestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Cultural Work Manifestation\" class represents cultural objects and productions that fall outside the traditional Western concept of \"artistic\" objects. This class encompasses a wide range of cultural works that are significant in their own right but do not fit the specific connotations and constructions associated with the Western concept of art. Examples include traditional crafts, indigenous artifacts, cultural rituals, folkloric expressions, community-based creations, and other forms of cultural manifestations. The purpose of this class is to provide a more inclusive framework for classifying and understanding cultural productions that cannot be categorized as \"artworks\" within the Western paradigm."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Work_Manifestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "cultural work manifestation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Cultural_Work_Manifestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "objeto cultural"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curation
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conception> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid201 .
_:genid201 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Time_Range> .
_:genid201 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#hasTimeSpan> .
_:genid201 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Curation\" class represents the process and practice of selecting, organizing, and presenting artworks and other cultural and material objects within an art exhibition. This includes all activities related to the conceptual aspects of creating a cohesive and meaningful exhibition, such as research, selection of works, thematic development, arrangement of artworks, and interpretative content."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "curación"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "curation"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curator
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Author> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid202 .
_:genid202 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> _:genid203 .
_:genid203 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:genid205 .
_:genid205 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:genid204 .
_:genid204 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
