_:genid202 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Curator\" class represents individuals or entities responsible for the conceptualization of exhibition-curatorial projects. Curators play a crucial role in the selection of exhibition themes, development of curatorial discourse, selection of exhibitors and works, and interpretation of cultural objects. Curators may work independently or as part of a team within museums, galleries, or other cultural institutions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "comisario"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "curator"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Discourse
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Discourse> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Discourse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Discourse> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Discourse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This class refers to the narrative, critical thinking, and conceptual framework developed by curators to guide the creation, organization, and interpretation of an exhibition. This discourse encompasses the thematic, theoretical, and contextual elements that shape the presentation and understanding of the artworks or artifacts on display."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Discourse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "curatorial discourse"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Discourse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "discurso curatorial"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Proposal
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Proposal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Proposal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Ideas> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Proposal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid206 .
_:genid206 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Curatorial_Project> .
_:genid206 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#isPreliminaryIdeasOf> .
_:genid206 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Proposal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Curatorial Proposal designates a propositional entity that sets out a curatorial project in a preliminary, projective form. It articulates the intended concept, scope, rationale, and curatorial approach—often including aims, selection principles, thematic lines, key references, and practical constraints—so that the project can be discussed, evaluated, negotiated, or commissioned prior to its realization."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Proposal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "curatorial proposal"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Proposal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "propuesta de comisariado"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Work
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Work> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Conceptual_Work> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This class refers to the comprehensive conceptualization, planning, and organization of a cultural activity and production based on selection processes and narrative building. This project encompasses various actions and processes, including the conceptualization of the curatorial discourse and narrative to be unfolded, the selection of activities to be carried out or material objects to be displayed or recorded, coordination with participants, the design of the associated place (digital and/or physical), and the development of interpretative content."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "curatorial project"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "proyecto curatorial"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Database
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Database> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Database> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Computational_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Database> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Information_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Database> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Work_Manifestation> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Database> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "base de datos"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Database> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "database"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Database> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#modelingNote> "Modeling guideline: Use Database as Information_Object (and as Computational_Object when relevant) when it is modeled primarily as an informational and/or technical resource. Add typing as Work_Manifestation only when the database is modeled as a released, citable manifestation (e.g., curated edition, versioned release, DOI or equivalent publication framing, circulation and reception)."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Date
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Date> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Date> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Time_Span> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Date> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Temporal unit that does not imply duration. This class represents a specific point in time identified by a day, usually recorded as year, month, and day."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Date> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "date"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Date> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fecha"@es .
