<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Exhibition\" class represents a curated display of artworks, artifacts, or cultural items presented to the public in a specific venue, such as a museum, gallery, or cultural center. Exhibitions are organized to showcase collections, promote artistic expression, educate audiences, and engage the public with cultural heritage."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "exhibition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "exposición"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Curatorial_Project
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Curatorial_Project> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Curatorial_Project> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Curatorial_Work> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Curatorial_Project> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid213 .
_:genid213 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition> .
_:genid213 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#hasManifestation> .
_:genid213 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Curatorial_Project> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This class refers to the comprehensive conceptualization, planning, and organization of an art exhibition. This project encompasses various activities, including the conceptualization of the curatorial discourse, the selection of works to be displayed, the coordination with artists, the design and layout of the exhibition space, the development of interpretative content, and the formulation of audience engagement strategies."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Curatorial_Project> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "exhibition curatorial project"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Curatorial_Project> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "proyecto expositivo-curatorial"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Idea
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Idea> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Idea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Ideas> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Idea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid214 .
_:genid214 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Curatorial_Project> .
_:genid214 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#isPreliminaryIdeasOf> .
_:genid214 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Idea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Exhibition Idea designates a preliminary propositional entity expressing an initial concept for an exhibition. It typically outlines a core intuition—such as a theme, question, or curatorial premise—and may include early indications of scope, potential works or materials, and intended modes of presentation. It functions as an early-stage articulation that can be developed into a curatorial proposal, refined through research and discussion, or abandoned."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Idea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "exhibition idea"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Idea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "idea de exposición"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Making
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Making> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Making> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/E12_Production> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Making> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid215 .
_:genid215 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Time_Range> .
_:genid215 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#hasTimeSpan> .
_:genid215 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Making> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Exhibition Making\" class represents the comprehensive set of activities aimed at the effective production of an art exhibition. This encompasses the materialization of a curatorial and exhibition project, including the planning, coordination, and execution of all tasks necessary to bring the exhibition to life. Activities within Exhibition Making involve collaboration between curators, artists, designers, museographers, experts in visual branding, and other stakeholders to ensure the successful realization of the exhibition's vision."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Making> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "exhibition making"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibition_Making> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "producción expositiva"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibitionary_Event
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibitionary_Event> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibitionary_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#propositional_activity> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibitionary_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Exhibitionary Event\" class represents any event specifically organized to showcase artworks, artifacts, or cultural items to the public. These events can include art exhibitions, gallery openings, art fairs, and other similar occasions where the primary focus is the presentation and viewing of curated collections."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibitionary_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "evento expositivo"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibitionary_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "exhibitionary event"@en .
