# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Expansion_Dispositif
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Expansion_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Expansion_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Dispositif> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Expansion_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Expansion Dispositif\" class represents propositional objects and activities used to expand the interpretation, readings, understanding, and overall comprehension of cultural activities and productions. These dispositifs include supplementary materials, interactive media, extended narratives, academic publications, discussion forums, and other materials and activities designed to deepen and broaden the audience's engagement and understanding of the cultural activities and productions. Additionally, other propositional objects and activities can also serve this purpose. Therefore, this class links cultural activities and productions with those propositional objects and activities that expand their understanding and interpretations, regardless of their nature, genre, or typology."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Expansion_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dispositivo de expansión"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Expansion_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "expansion dispositif"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Expansion_Dispositif> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#modelingNote> "This class is not disjoint with other dispositif types; see Dispositif modeling note."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Fair
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Fair> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Fair> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Exhibitionary_Event> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Fair> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid216 .
