# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Material_Object
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Material_Object> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Material_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Material_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Material Object\" class encompasses entities that have a material existence in the world, either as physical objects or as formal realizations or materializations of ideas, concepts, etc. This class includes both physical and digital entities, as well as entities that exist solely as formal expressions, such as a poem or a melody. Material Objects are characterized by their tangible or representational form, making them accessible to perception, interaction, or representation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Material_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "material object"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Material_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "objeto material"@es .
