# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Mediation_Dispositif
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Mediation_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Mediation_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Dispositif> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Mediation_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Mediation Dispositif\" class represents propositional objects and activities used to facilitate the interpretation, understanding, and engagement with cultural activities and productions. These dispositifs typically include educational materials, guided tours, interactive displays, workshops, and other structured systems or tools that mediate the relationship between the audience and the cultural activity and production. Additionally, other propositional objects and activities can also serve this purpose. Therefore, this class links cultural activities and productions with those propositional objects and activities that mediate with the audience, regardless of their nature, genre, or typology."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Mediation_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dispositivo de mediación"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Mediation_Dispositif> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mediation dispositif"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Mediation_Dispositif> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#modelingNote> "This class is not disjoint with other dispositif types; see Dispositif modeling note."@en .
