# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Membership
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Membership> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Membership> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#professional_context> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Membership> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Membership is an intermediary (reified) spatio-temporal context that models the relationship by which an individual or collective human actant participates as a member of a group or corporate body. It represents membership as historically contingent rather than permanent, allowing the association of the member and the membership organisation with a defined time range and, where relevant, with additional qualifying terms (e.g., type of membership, status, or conditions of participation). In OntoExhibit, Membership supports the analysis of institutional and collective engagement by making membership explicit, queryable, and comparable across different organisations and periods.\n\nThis class is broader than foaf:membershipClass, which constrains membership organisations to instances of foaf:Group. In OntoExhibit, the category of Collective Human Actant encompasses both groups and corporate bodies, and either may function as a membership organisation; Membership therefore provides a more flexible pattern aligned with exhibition ecosystems and their heterogeneous organisational forms."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Membership> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "membership"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Membership> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "membresía"@es .
