# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Organization_Schema
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Organization_Schema> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Organization_Schema> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/E28_Conceptual_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Organization_Schema> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An abstract organization schema that specifies how parts, units, or elements are arranged and related within an intellectual work or exhibition-related articulation. It provides an explicit pattern of ordering (e.g., sequences, groupings, hierarchies, modules) through which content can be structured, independently of the media or dispositifs through which it may later be realized."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Organization_Schema> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "estructura de ordenación"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Organization_Schema> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ordering structure"@en .
