# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Place_Of_Residence
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Place_Of_Residence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Place_Of_Residence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#biographical_context> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Place_Of_Residence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Residency is an intermediary (reified) spatio-temporal context that links a person to a place where they reside for a given time range. It is designed to represent residential history as a sequence of time-qualified relations rather than as a fixed attribute, allowing multiple residences to be recorded for the same individual across different periods. By capturing when and where a person lived, Residency supports the analysis of biographical trajectories, mobility patterns, and the spatial distribution of life contexts over time."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Place_Of_Residence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "residencia"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Place_Of_Residence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "residency"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Planned_Activity
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Planned_Activity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Planned_Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Activity> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Planned_Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Planned Activity\" class represents any type of event that is systematically scheduled and organized ahead of time, often of significant interest, that takes place at a specific time and location. This includes a wide range of activities such as exhibitions, performances, lectures, workshops, openings, and other cultural or social gatherings. These activities are characterized by their temporality, purpose, and the involvement of participants or an audience. They are organized to achieve specific objectives, such as education, entertainment, community engagement, or celebration."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Planned_Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "actividad programada"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Planned_Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "planned activity"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Ideas
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Ideas> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Ideas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/E28_Conceptual_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Ideas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Ideas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Preliminary Ideas\" class represents the initial and preliminary concepts, thesis, arguments, hypothesis… that precede and ground the conception of a complete work. This can materialize as drafts, sketches, briefings, provisional reports, and other preparatory documents and artifacts. Preliminary Ideas serve as the foundational elements and exploratory steps in the conceptual, intellectual, and creative process, capturing the early stages of ideation, planning, and conceptual development. This class enables the analysis of changes and modifications experienced by works during their conceptualization process."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Ideas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ideas preliminares"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Ideas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "preliminary ideas"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Propositional_Object
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Propositional_Object> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Propositional_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Propositional_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Preliminary Propositional Object\" class represents entities that capture initial ideas, drafts, sketches, and other preliminary forms of a conceptual work. These objects are characterized by their formative nature, documenting the early stages of the creative or planning process. Preliminary Propositional Objects are crucial for understanding the development and evolution of a work, as they provide insights into the creator's thought process, experimentation, and conceptual groundwork. Examples include draft manuscripts, rough sketches, conceptual diagrams, provisional reports, and brainstorming notes."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Propositional_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "objeto proposicional preliminar"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Preliminary_Propositional_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "preliminary propositional object"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Event
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Event> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Communication_Activity> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid244 .
_:genid244 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Date> .
_:genid244 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#hasTimeSpan> .
_:genid244 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Press Event\" class represents a media-focused event organized to provide information, announcements, or updates to journalists, media representatives, and other stakeholders. This includes press conferences, media briefings, and other events specifically designed to engage the press and provide them with the necessary materials and information to report on exhibitions, new acquisitions, significant developments, or special events."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "press conference"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "rueda de prensa"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Release
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Release> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Release> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Linguistic_Information_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Release> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "press release"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Press_Release> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "nota de prensa" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Produced_Material_Object
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Produced_Material_Object> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Produced_Material_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Material_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Produced_Material_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Produced Material Object\" class represents material objects that have been intentionally brought into material existence or manufactured through human effort or technological processes, with potential collaboration of non-human agents. These objects encompass a wide range of items, including physical artifacts, digital products, and formal expressions of ideas or concepts. Produced Material Objects are characterized by their origin in a production process, which can involve artistic creation, industrial manufacturing, digital rendering, computational programming, or other forms of materialization."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Produced_Material_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "produced material object"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Producer
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Producer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Producer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Role> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Producer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "producer"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Producer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "productor"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Professional_Association
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Professional_Association> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Professional_Association> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F11_Corporate_Body> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Professional_Association> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An organizational entity that unites individuals from a specific profession with the aim of supporting continuous professional development, and representing the interests of its members in the public sphere. Examples of professional associations relevant in the art exhibition domain are “Asociación de Artistas Visuales (AAV)” or “Asociación de Galerías de Arte de Andalucía (AGAA)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Professional_Association> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "asociación profesional"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Professional_Association> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "professional association"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Project_Director
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Project_Director> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Project_Director> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Role> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Project_Director> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "director/a de proyecto"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Project_Director> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "project director"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Promoter
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Promoter> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Promoter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Role> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Promoter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "promoter"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Promoter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "promotor"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/E28_Conceptual_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This class refers to a semantic, intellectual, or conceptual element that articulates specific ideas. It can take the form of assertions, theses, hypotheses, arguments, interpretations, among others. Propositions are inherently part of \"propositional entities.\" They can be developed through “conceptual works”, conveyed and embodied in propositional objects, and assigned to any entity."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "proposición"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "proposition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#modelingNote> "Proposition is propositional content. It is related to conceptual objects  via conveys and for propositional objects via embodies."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition_Assignment
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition_Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition_Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Assignment> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition_Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Proposition Assignment\" class represents the action of assigning a proposition, which can include interpretations, valuations, critical assessment, or other similar statements to an entity. This process involves linking specific propositions to artworks, exhibitions, objects, or any relevant subjects, thereby providing additional context, meaning, or evaluation. Proposition assignments are essential for enriching the understanding and appreciation of entities within the domain, facilitating scholarly analysis, and supporting curatorial decisions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition_Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "asignación de proposición"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Proposition_Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "proposition assignment"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Entity
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Entity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Propositional Entity\" class represents any entity, whether conceptual, material, or activity-based, that conveys, embodies, or entails some form of proposition. This proposition can be intentional and explicit or implicit. Propositional Entities encompass a wide range of forms, including artworks, exhibitions, catalogs, literary works, scholarly works, performances, lectures, conferences, and other entities that communicate or represent specific meanings, concepts, or messages. These entities are characterized by their capacity to convey and embody propositional content, which may involve thesis, hypotheses, interpretations, critical discussions, etc."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "entidad proposicional"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "propositional entity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Entity> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#modelingNote> "Propositional_Entity is used as a transversal category for entities that bear one or more propositions as their propositional content. It does not introduce a separate “kind” of thing, but marks a shared capacity across different branches of the ontology (e.g., conceptual works, preliminary ideas, propositional objects, or planned activities) to be related to Proposition."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Object
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Object> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Produced_Material_Object> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Propositional Object\" class represents material entities that are realizations of ideas, concepts, or conceptual works. Propositional Objects are characterized by their semantic nature. They convey meaning, express intellectual concepts, or articulate discourses. They can take the form of physical objects, formal expressions, or digital entities."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "objeto proposicional"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Propositional_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "propositional object"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Public
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Public> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Public> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Role> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Public> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "public"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Public> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "público"@es .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publication
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publication> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publication> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/7.1.1/E12_Production> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publication> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid245 .
_:genid245 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Territorial_Entity> .
_:genid245 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#takesPlaceAt> .
_:genid245 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publication> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This class comprises the processes and activities of publishing. This process involves various stages, including the creation, editing, design, printing or digital formatting. Publication brings into material existence propositional objects in the form of books, journals, articles, reports, catalogs, brochures, and digital content such as e-books or online articles."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publication> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "publicación"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publication> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "publication"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publication> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> "https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F30"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publisher
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publisher> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publisher> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Company> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publisher> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Role> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publisher> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Publisher"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publisher> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "editor (publisher)"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publisher> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "firma editorial"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Publisher> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "publisher"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Representation
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Representation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Representation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#professional_context> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Representation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Representation is an intermediary (reified) spatio-temporal context that models the formal relationship in which an organisation—typically an art gallery—represents an artist or an artists’ collective. It captures the fact that representation is historically contingent and may change over time, enabling the association of the represented actant and the representing organisation with a specific time range (and, when relevant, with particular territories or market contexts). In OntoExhibit, Representation supports the analysis of professional networks and institutional mediation, covering activities such as promotion, market brokerage (e.g., sales), and the coordination of exhibition opportunities, without reducing these complex dynamics to a simple, timeless link between artist and gallery."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Representation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "representación"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Representation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "representation"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Research_Assistant
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Research_Assistant> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Research_Assistant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Assistant> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Research_Assistant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ayudante de investigación"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Research_Assistant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "research assistant"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Role
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Role> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "rol"@es .
