# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Vernissage
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Vernissage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Vernissage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Beginning_Of_Activity> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Vernissage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid251 .
_:genid251 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Date> .
_:genid251 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#hasTimeSpan> .
_:genid251 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Vernissage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Vernissage\" class represents the private viewing or preview of an art exhibition, typically held before the official opening to the public. Vernissages are often exclusive events attended by invited guests such as artists, critics, collectors, and other VIPs. These events provide an opportunity for attendees to view the artworks in an intimate setting, often accompanied by speeches, performances, or social gatherings that celebrate the launch of the exhibition."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Vernissage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "vernissage"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Vernissage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "vernissage"@es .
