# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Visual_Organization_Schema
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Visual_Organization_Schema> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Visual_Organization_Schema> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Organization_Schema> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Visual_Organization_Schema> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An ordering structure that specifies visual and spatial patterns of arrangement (e.g., layout logics, visual hierarchies, grids, pathways, alignments, groupings) through which content is made legible or navigable. It captures the schema of visual organization independently of any particular material installation or interface."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Visual_Organization_Schema> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "organización visual"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Visual_Organization_Schema> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "visual organization schema"@en .
