# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Website
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Website> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Website> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Digital_Place> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Website> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The \"Website\" class represents a collection of web pages and related content identified by a common domain name and published on at least one web server. In the art exhibition domain, examples include museums' websites that host digital exhibitions and other digital resources related to exhibitions, as well as websites specifically designed for an exhibition, such as the website of the digital exhibition Iconoclash (2023)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Website> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "website"@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Website> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "website"@es .
