# https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#spatio-temporal_context
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#spatio-temporal_context> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#spatio-temporal_context> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Spatio-temporal context is a superclass for intermediary (reified) constructs that qualify relationships by explicitly attaching them to a time range and, when relevant, to a spatial setting or other contextual parameters. It is used to model situations in which a link between an actant (person, collective, institution) and an entity such as a place, an organization, a role, or a position must be expressed as historically variable rather than fixed. Instances of this class therefore function as contextual “records” that capture how a relationship holds during a specific period (and potentially in specific locations), supporting the representation of change over time (e.g., moving residence, shifting memberships, evolving professional affiliations, or relocating areas of activity).\n\nIn OntoExhibit, Spatio-temporal context provides a shared modeling pattern for biographical and professional/institutional histories—such as Residency, Place of Activity, Membership, Representation, Executive Position, and Affiliation—by separating the stable entities involved (actants, places, organizations) from the time-qualified contexts that connect them. This design enables robust querying and comparative analysis of trajectories, networks, and spatial distributions across the exhibition ecosystem without conflating entities with the temporalized circumstances in which their relations are enacted."@en .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#spatio-temporal_context> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "contexto espacio-temporal"@es .
<https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#spatio-temporal_context> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "spatio-temporal context"@en .
