# https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F11_Corporate_Body
<https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F11_Corporate_Body> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F11_Corporate_Body> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/OntoExhibit#Collective_Human_Actant> .
<https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F11_Corporate_Body> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A \"Corporate Body\" refers to an organization or group of individuals that is recognized by law as a single entity, having its own legal identity separate from that of its members. This class encompasses entities such as corporations, associations, institutions, and government agencies, which can own property, enter into contracts, sue, and be sued in their own name. The corporate body operates through a structured governance system, typically including a board of directors or similar governing body, and is established for specific purposes such as business, education, or public service. The definition of a corporate body highlights its capacity to act as a unified entity in legal, financial, and operational contexts."@en .
<https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F11_Corporate_Body> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "corporate body"@en .
<https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F11_Corporate_Body> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "organismo corporativo"@es .
<https://www.iflastandards.info/fr/frbr/frbroo#F11_Corporate_Body> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> "http://xmlns.com/foaf/spec/#term_Group"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
